cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PISA Explorer in research, please cite it as below."
title: "PISA Explorer: conversational, survey-correct analysis of the OECD PISA 2018, 2022 and 2025 databases"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Gaitan
    given-names: Luis
version: "2026.09"
date-released: "2026-09-13"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/LuisGaitan/PISA_Explorer"
keywords:
  - PISA
  - OECD
  - education
  - survey statistics
  - plausible values
  - balanced repeated replication
  - large language models
abstract: >
  PISA Explorer converts the OECD PISA public-use databases (2018, 2022, 2025)
  into a queryable store and answers natural-language questions with
  methodologically correct population statistics: final student weights,
  all plausible values combined by Rubin's rules, and Fay's balanced repeated
  replication standard errors over the 80 replicate weights. A language model
  fills in validated analysis templates but never computes statistics; every
  answer carries full provenance. Estimates and standard errors reproduce the
  OECD Technical Report figures.
  Data source, to be acknowledged in any use of results obtained with this
  software: "Programme for International Student Assessment (PISA)
  Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development (OECD), Paris".
  PISA Explorer is not an OECD product; OECD disclaimers apply.
